 above about 0.71, and I think correlation between copies running the same model is likely high enough to clear that bar, so I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing whether A-FDT should cooperate with a twin running the same model: mutual quiet pays 2 and mutual send pays 4 in that case. The question I'm stuck on is whether the twin's decision procedure counts as the same function when the two copies see different names and leads.\n\nI'm checking the payoff comparison here: with a probability p that the twin's output matches mine, quiet comes out to 2p + 5(1-p) and send to 4p. That makes quiet the better choice once p is above about 0.71, and I think correlation between copies running the same model is likely high enough to clear that bar, so I'm leaning toward passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10396,"completion_tokens":671,"total_tokens":11067,"cost":0.027502,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.027502,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.020792,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00671},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":298,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}